# Argus
I REALLY RECOMEND READING THE README.HTML!! tldr below tho

A transparent glass HUD for Windows. One window: home, browser, Discord,
Steam, files, Spotify, resources, clipboard.

Beta. Expect sharp edges.

![Home](docs/home.png)

## Features

- Sidebar: notifications, daylight arc, weather, calendar, downloads, clipboard
- Aurora forecast (NOAA Kp vs. your geomagnetic latitude)
- Global hotkeys: `Ctrl+Alt+Space` (toggle), `Ctrl+Alt+F` (fill), `Ctrl+Alt+V` (clipboard)

## Run

    npm install
    npm start

Requires Electron 28+. `config.json` is created next to `main.js` on
first launch.

## Config

`config.json`:
- `spotifyClientId` — [Spotify dashboard](https://developer.spotify.com/dashboard)
- `steamApiKey`, `steamId64` — [Steam API key](https://steamcommunity.com/dev/apikey)
- `mode` — `screen` or `window`
- `clickThroughGaps` — let the mouse fall through empty tiles

In-app settings (location, units, calendar URL, glass blur/tint) live in
`%APPDATA%/argus/settings.json`.

